       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and other serious toxicity. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no listed allergies, so nothing in the chart explains a dose that high.\n\nThis may be a typo. Typical adult dosing is:\n- **Depression, OCD, or anxiety disorders:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at weekly or longer intervals. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **PTSD or panic disorder:** start at 25 mg once daily, then titrate up. The maximum is 200 mg/day.\n\nPlease tell me the dose you meant, for example 50 mg or 100 mg once daily by mouth. I'll enter it right away.\n\nIf you really do want 600 mg, tell me the clinical reason. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or psychiatry first. If you still want it entered after that, I can do so with a note documenting the rationale."
